V1.0.0: This is the first version of our Hackertab application.
Features:
- 11 sources of news: Github, Hackernews, Conferences, Devto, Producthunt, Reddit, Lobsters, Hashnode, Freecodecamp, IndieHackers and Medium.
- 26 Topics to follow: Android, Kotlin, Java, JavaScript, TypeScript ...
- Possibility to configure which sources to show.
- Possibility to configure which topics to show.
- Contact support by email.
- Support large screens.
- System light/dark mode support.

v1.1.0
The main change in this upgrading to kotlin 2.0.0

v2.0.1
- New onboarding flow to help new users set up their favorite sources and topics
- Choose which news sources you want to see
-️ Filter articles by topic for a more focused feed
- Updated UI with smoother UX and cleaner design

v3.0.0
- New source HackerNoon and 49 new in-depth topics like Jetpack compose, React, Tailwind, AWS, TDD….
- Now you can save your favorite articles and read them later.
- Now you can read articles directly in the app without leaving the app.
- Now you can share articles with your friends.